4 days of 12 hours: six of cheap wind, then six of none.
full foresight   one window                      cost  62400.00   peak soc  120.0

rolling  length=8   step=8   lookahead=0   windows  6   cost  74000.00   peak soc   90.0   + 18.6%
rolling  length=12  step=8   lookahead=4   windows  6   cost  68000.00   peak soc  120.0   +  9.0%
rolling  length=16  step=8   lookahead=8   windows  6   cost  62400.00   peak soc  120.0   +  0.0%

The store cycles in every schedule — this is not a model where storage
stops being worth having. What myopia costs is the end of each window:
charge a window cannot spend before its horizon runs out is worth
nothing to it, so it arrives empty and the next window starts from zero.
Lookahead gives it somewhere to spend that charge, and the gap closes.

every schedule above covers all 48 snapshots exactly once
